# C049 — TOOLFACTORY ADOPTION ROADMAP (plan only; operator chose "record the roadmap, build later"). toolfactory is the
# reference dogfood that proves the C038-C048 packages under real money-bearing load; already a PARTIAL dogfood (deps
# @suluk/{core,cost,harden,journeys,sdk,stripe,testgen,...} + api/journeys/*.feature). Adoption = replace the remaining
# hand-rolled code with the packages, in RISK order. THREE PHASES: (A) audit+BDD LOW-risk — scripts/ci-*/checklist-gate ->
# @suluk/cockpit conformanceGates (C045); api/journeys/*.feature -> @suluk/journeys audit/demos/promote (C040/C042/C043);
# readiness/settlement -> harden auditReadiness (C043) + cost settlementAudit (C044). (B) provisioning MEDIUM-risk —
# scripts/provision*.ts + mint-*.ts + sync-secrets.ts -> a provision.config.ts + @suluk/provision brokers + generate/
# migrate (C047), collapses ~700 LOC. (C) runtime HIGH-risk MONEY (its own dedicated parity-tested pass) — api/src/
# credits.ts -> @suluk/credits, key-lineage.ts+apikeys.ts -> @suluk/keys, billing.ts+pricing.ts -> @suluk/billing+@suluk/
# payments. C IS the money cutover every C046/C048 ADR flagged: migrate FUNCTION-BY-FUNCTION behind a parity test (same DB
# effect / same Stripe request), never at the tail of other work; the atomic-debit CAS + pooled cap + idempotent grant are
# load-bearing. STAYS APP (not a gap): webhook DISPATCH, pricing MATRIX, subscription-pooling+refund workflow, alerts/email,
# the Stripe-PLATFORM ops (hosted Checkout/saved-card mgmt/subscription CRUD/Tax). Sequence A->B->C; A+B independently
# shippable; recommend an ADR per phase at build time (C050+). DESIGNED-not-built => ceiling 0.5.
claim toolfactory_adoption_roadmap_three_phases_money_cutover_last: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when toolfactory_adoption_roadmap_three_phases_money_cutover_last == False
